#X text 12 964 raw 1 - pin gate/peak and take `reg <addr> <data>` chip-bus writes (see vgm~). raw 0 - back to normal;
#X obj 12 1004 cnv 3 696 3 empty empty carrier table - who is audible per alg 8 12 0 13 -228856 -1 0;
#X text 12 1024 alg 0;
#X text 90 1024 op1>op3>op2>op4 - carrier op4;
#X text 12 1040 alg 1;
#X text 90 1040 (op1+op3)>op2>op4 - carrier op4;
#X text 12 1056 alg 2;
#X text 90 1056 op1>op4 and op3>op2>op4 - carrier op4;
#X text 12 1072 alg 3;
#X text 90 1072 op1>op3>op4 and op2>op4 - carrier op4;
#X text 12 1088 alg 4;
#X text 90 1088 (op1>op3) + (op2>op4) - carriers op3 op4;
#X text 12 1104 alg 5;
#X text 90 1104 op1>(op2 op3 op4) - carriers op2 op3 op4;
#X text 12 1120 alg 6;
#X text 90 1120 (op1>op3) + op2 + op4 - carriers op2 op3 op4;
#X text 12 1136 alg 7;
#X text 90 1136 all four direct - carriers op1 op2 op3 op4;
#X text 12 1160 ADSR: the overall envelope = the CARRIER ops' envelope. Modulator envelopes shape timbre only.;
#X text 12 1178 so: alg 0-3 tune op 4 only. alg 4 tune op 3 + op 4. alg 5-6 tune op 2-4. alg 7 tune op 1-4.;
#X text 12 1196 pluck: ar 31 dr 18 sl 15 rr 15 per carrier (sl 15 = decay to silence). pad: ar 20 dr 5 sl 0 sr 0 rr 10;
#X text 12 1214 OUTLETS (all signal): 0 = the six chip channels summed - patch through a gain into dac~. 1..6 = channels 1..6 alone (ch1 = the note/GM voice \, raw mode fills all six). There is NO output clip: dense multi-channel sums can exceed +-1 \, the final gain owns that headroom. Compare rr with the gate toggle.;
#X text 12 1240 PER-CHANNEL VOICES: chN <msg> (N = 1..6) addresses chip channel N directly - each channel is its own voice on its own outlet;
#X text 12 1258 ch1 note 60 100 / ch2 note 41 90 / ch2 gm 41 / ch3 alg 7 / ch4 op 4 ar 31 / ch5 gate 1 - the same messages \, per channel. chN note off (vel 0) releases just that channel;
#X text 12 1276 chN reg <addr> <data> = channel-addressed raw register write (bytes verbatim \, the port resolved by N \, key-on rides port A as on silicon);
#X text 12 1294 a never-addressed channel carries the factory voice and sounds on its first note\; chN gm swaps its preset. Bare spellings always mean channel 1;
#X text 12 1312 dac / raw / bank are object-global settings - the chN prefix is accepted but has no per-channel meaning for them;
#X text 420 900 glide/slide (portamento);
